# <fs>          <mountpoint>  <type>  <opts>                      <dump> <pass>
# No root line and no /data line (MAINLINE-STEP2-DESIGN review F7): a line by
# LABEL= or UUID= is not unique once both slots hold mainline (system_a and
# system_b hold the same image, with the same label and UUID), and mount -a
# could then mount the other slot's root file system or a second data file
# system.
# root: the initramfs mounts the partition with the GPT name of the booted
# slot (system_a or system_b, 1792 MiB, ext4 label tsxroot) with
# rw,noatime,commit=60, after it checked it and grew it to fill the partition.
# data: the service uc-pxx-lvm mounts /data before localmount, by device and
# with an exact label check (ext4 label tsxdata): the partition with the GPT
# name userdata (phase 2), else the LVM volume tsx/data over vendor_a and
# oem_a (phase 1). Without either, everything lives on the root file system.
tmpfs           /tmp          tmpfs   nosuid,nodev,mode=1777      0      0
